     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day total)\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency\n- **Extended-release metformin**, which has a maximum of 2,000 mg/day, usually given once daily with the evening meal\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm that. I can enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose, though I'd advise against it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
